WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.290
- All right everybody, please welcome

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:05.942
2020 Olympic gold medalist,
Tamyra Mensah-Stock.

00:00:05.942 --> 00:00:07.692
(everyone applauding)

00:00:07.692 --> 00:00:09.338
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.338 --> 00:00:12.303
(woman gives high scream)

00:00:12.303 --> 00:00:13.600
Oh my gosh,

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.070
I need to tell you I'm
one of your biggest fans,

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.240
just from that interview.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.030
Like, if you haven't seen
the whole interview already

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:19.880
you've got to watch it.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.090
I love the whole Carrie
Underwood Champion song,

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:25.320
I love the whole thing, I
thought it was so great.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.940
Congratulations on your gold medal

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.225
and meet Beth, Deidre and Rob.

00:00:30.225 --> 00:00:32.324
(crowd cheering)

00:00:32.324 --> 00:00:34.410
I've been nerding out.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.990
Okay, so you spoke about
your dad in that video

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:38.760
and sadly he passed away
when you're in high school,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.287
but what was he like at your events?

00:00:40.287 --> 00:00:41.963
Like your tournaments before?

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:44.420
- Like I said, in the interview,

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.840
he was definitely one of loudest people,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.170
if not the loudest
person in the auditorium.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:54.067
Every single competition
or dual, he'd always yell,

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:56.892
"Kill them, Kill them, Kill them!".

00:00:56.892 --> 00:00:58.643
(everyone laughs)

00:00:58.643 --> 00:01:00.367
And right after done with
the match I'd tell him,

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.040
"Daddy, you're not supposed to say that,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.432
I'm not supposed to kill them,

00:01:03.432 --> 00:01:05.360
I'm just supposed to
pin them and beat them".

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.880
He was like, "No, you go out
there and you go kill them.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.372
That's what you do."

00:01:09.372 --> 00:01:10.205
I was like ah.

00:01:10.205 --> 00:01:11.038
(crowd applauding)

00:01:11.038 --> 00:01:12.819
- Oh my gosh, I love that.

00:01:12.819 --> 00:01:13.999
(crowd cheering)

00:01:13.999 --> 00:01:16.500
Wait so, your dad cheered you on,

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.340
but I hear you have something that you do

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.120
before events, right?

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:25.120
- Yes, before I go into competitions,

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.000
I like to settle my nerves

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.990
by singing karaoke.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:32.678
And I think it's a great
way to just express,

00:01:32.678 --> 00:01:35.600
(raspy scream)

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:38.470
just express myself and basically

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.770
alleviate a lot of stress
from everybody else.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.290
And I had a lot of people join in on fun,

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.920
and I actually brought a karaoke machine

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.200
to the Kanagawa, in Tokyo, in Japan,

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.480
because I knew I was just gonna be,

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.920
you know, under a lot of stress.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.010
I didn't wanna feel that,

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.160
and so I brought a karaoke machine.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.640
And one of the songs that
I actually got to sing,

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:03.399
that I love singing, is
songs by you ,so it was-

00:02:03.399 --> 00:02:04.470
- What song?

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.436
- It's "Because of You", that's
the song that I love to do.

00:02:07.436 --> 00:02:09.302
(everyone laughing)

00:02:09.302 --> 00:02:10.135
- Wait!

00:02:10.135 --> 00:02:12.290
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.543
That is like a super depressing song.

00:02:16.883 --> 00:02:19.503
That is a super depressing
song to get you amped up.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:22.960
- The song, it's me talking about my past,

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.590
like talking to my past self,

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:26.699
and all the mistakes that
I've made and just basically

00:02:26.699 --> 00:02:29.000
(sound cuts out)

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.640
I know what I've been through

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.980
and I'm going to come out it,
and I'm gonna get stronger,

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.010
and I'm going to move forward.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.078
Why? Because of you.

00:02:37.078 --> 00:02:37.911
And it's a great song!

00:02:37.911 --> 00:02:38.744
- [Kelly] Oh I love that!-

00:02:38.744 --> 00:02:39.577
- Come on.

00:02:39.577 --> 00:02:40.410
(crowd applauding)

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.243
(Tamyra singing)

00:02:41.243 --> 00:02:42.705
- ♪ I've learned the hard way
that fist fights start with, ♪

00:02:42.705 --> 00:02:43.930
♪ Because of you ♪

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.721
♪ I never stray to far from the sidewalk ♪

00:02:47.721 --> 00:02:49.607
(crowd Cheering)

00:02:49.607 --> 00:02:51.880
- That's my favorite thing
to learn about people.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.100
Like you write a song
and it's about your own

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:57.420
whatever going on and
then how people take songs

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.480
and they really apply them to themselves.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:00.660
Like it's incredible.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.140
That's so cool, I've never
thought of that song like-

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:03.360
I'm gonna start thinking of it that way,

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.682
cause my way is real depressing.

00:03:05.682 --> 00:03:07.630
- [Kelly] ♪ Muh muh muh ♪

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:10.730
But we we have a girl backstage

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:13.110
whose dream is to be the next Tamyra.

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:15.090
She's 12 and already winning tournaments

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.070
across the state of California.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.270
So cute.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.840
Her dream is to win
gold just like her hero.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:22.240
She looks tough y'all.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.050
She has no idea to Tamyra is with us,

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.797
or that Tamyra has a surprise in store.

00:03:27.797 --> 00:03:31.160
We'll bring to Tamyra
backup on the monitor

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.850
whenever it's time, but
we want to surprise her.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.503
So stick around everybody.
You don't want to miss this.

00:03:35.503 --> 00:03:36.336
(everyone applauding)

00:03:36.336 --> 00:03:39.470
Joining us now is Velaria, a
12 year old wrestling phenom,

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:42.220
who's beating the pants
off girls and some boys

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.910
across California. I love her already.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:47.240
She's also a member of
the Beat The Streets,

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.150
an organization that promotes wrestling

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:50.800
in underserved communities.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.320
So Valeria. Hi.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.202
- Hey

00:03:53.202 --> 00:03:54.035
(crowd cheering)

00:03:54.035 --> 00:03:55.647
- And welcome her and meet everybody

00:03:55.647 --> 00:03:56.480
- Hi guys

00:03:58.027 --> 00:04:00.220
- So, okay you kicked
some serious but girl,

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.960
I've seen your stats. So
when did you start wrestling?

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.620
- I actually started
wrestling when I was in,

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:07.490
I was actually seven years
old when I started wrestling.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:10.142
I used to be a very girly girl at first,

00:04:10.142 --> 00:04:14.740
I really liked doing dance
and gymnastics and stuff,

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:16.820
but then right after
some of those practices,

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:19.820
I did have to go to practices
to go watch my brother,

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.474
cause you know, I had to do that. Yeah.

00:04:22.474 --> 00:04:23.820
(everyone laughing)

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:24.653
- My kids don't like it either

00:04:24.653 --> 00:04:26.231
when they have to watch the other.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.110
- But yeah, my mom did see that there was

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:33.220
some little, little girls,
like maybe like six, five,

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.700
starting to go to the practices and stuff

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:38.027
and there were really not
that many girls over there.

00:04:38.027 --> 00:04:38.860
- Yeah

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.253
- There was barely any.

00:04:41.276 --> 00:04:42.109
- Yeah

00:04:42.109 --> 00:04:44.313
- But after that, you know,

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.020
a couple of weeks later on

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:50.320
there was a tournament that
was going on and my coach

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.630
he was like, "Hey, do
you want to compete?"

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:54.090
And I said, "Sure, why not?
Let's just try it out".

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.020
Try it out.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:57.521
- Oh my Gosh, you're so cute look at you!

00:04:57.521 --> 00:05:00.700
(crowd applauding)

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:01.720
- It's truly amazing.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.440
So what inspires you to do this?

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.670
Like, especially you said
it's mostly boys, right?

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.520
What inspires you to keep doing this?

00:05:09.705 --> 00:05:12.970
- So my family is definitely one-

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:15.190
They're so supportive and I'm just

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.954
surrounded by so much love and support.

00:05:17.954 --> 00:05:21.250
And my biggest cheerleader
though is definitely my Abuela.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.731
- Oh, your Grandma, I love that.

00:05:23.731 --> 00:05:24.800
(crowd applauding)

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.640
Was she kind of like, cause I dunno,

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.500
for her generation it must've
been like, "Wait what,

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.041
you're doing what?" Was
she like that at first?

00:05:31.041 --> 00:05:31.925
- (laughing while saying) Yeah exactly,

00:05:31.925 --> 00:05:32.758
she was like, "What is that?"

00:05:32.758 --> 00:05:33.620
- Oh, I love that.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.817
- But she was, she was
always telling me like,

00:05:35.817 --> 00:05:38.220
"Go show those boys with a girl can do."

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:40.306
- Oh my gosh, I love your Grandma.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:41.956
(everyone applauding)

00:05:41.956 --> 00:05:43.666
How impressive is she?

00:05:43.666 --> 00:05:44.534
- Awesome, awesome

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:45.970
- Oh my gosh! I love it.

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:47.910
Well what's your ultimate dream?

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.600
- Well, my ultimate dream
is definitely to compete,

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.130
you know win gold in the Olympics.

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:54.968
- Go ahead, reach for it, yeah.

00:05:54.968 --> 00:05:57.776
(crowd cheering)

00:05:57.776 --> 00:06:01.200
I would definitely love
to place top three,

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.300
definitely top in the Olympics.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.740
- You love to win.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:07.010
- Just like Helen Maroulis.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:10.100
And you know, she I've seen
her wrestle she's amazing,

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:12.400
her technique is amazing,
She's pretty fast too.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:13.730
Her take-downs are really good too.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:16.660
- Yeah ,you know who I
love personally? Tamyra

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:17.730
Did you see Tamyra?

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:20.081
- Oh my gosh yes, she's amazing!

00:06:20.081 --> 00:06:23.010
Again, their techniques are
just, oh my gosh, amazing.

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:24.670
- Oh my gosh, so going for the gold.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:26.720
Well there's someone that I know,

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:29.150
who also believes, that
you have what it takes

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:30.230
to make it to the Olympics.

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:32.090
And I want you to meet her maybe.

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:33.626
So it's Tamyra Mensah-Stock!

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:34.459
(everyone applauding)

00:06:34.459 --> 00:06:35.634
- Oh my gosh.

00:06:35.634 --> 00:06:38.467
(crowd cheering)

00:06:40.102 --> 00:06:45.102
- Oh no, oh no, wait,

00:06:45.532 --> 00:06:48.199
oh no, here you go, here you go.

00:06:49.055 --> 00:06:51.388
Oh my gosh, she's losing it.

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:54.779
Oh!

00:06:55.761 --> 00:06:57.386
(man shouting "whoo")

00:06:57.386 --> 00:06:58.219
- Oh my gosh!

00:06:58.219 --> 00:07:00.713
- I love how happy you are.

00:07:00.713 --> 00:07:04.250
Go ahead Tamyra. What do
you wanna say to Valeria?

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:07.630
- Oh my gosh, Valeria,
I am so proud of you

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:10.380
for everything that you
accomplishing, for going out there

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:12.860
and making sure that nobody stops you,

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:15.040
because the only, the only person

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.477
that's gonna stop you is you.

00:07:16.477 --> 00:07:19.100
And you are so tough, I
can tell that not even you

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.077
are gonna be able to stop yourself.

00:07:20.077 --> 00:07:23.079
You're going to get first place.

00:07:23.079 --> 00:07:25.996
(crowd applauding)

00:07:27.206 --> 00:07:30.538
- Oh my gosh. I'm crying,
she's crying.It's contagious

00:07:30.538 --> 00:07:32.045
- Everything's fine.

00:07:32.045 --> 00:07:34.157
- Oh my gosh, that's awesome right?

00:07:34.157 --> 00:07:34.990
( people yelling "whoo")

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.722
- Oh my gosh, thank you so much.

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.047
That's a gold medalist
telling you, you can do it.

00:07:38.047 --> 00:07:40.066
You believe it, right?

00:07:40.066 --> 00:07:41.423
- Yeah, definitely.

00:07:41.423 --> 00:07:42.610
- All right, all right.

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:46.993
Well, you wanna stay in
touch with her, right?

00:07:48.797 --> 00:07:50.947
- Valeria, you know due to Safe Sport

00:07:50.947 --> 00:07:53.380
We have to make sure that you are safe

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:55.460
because you are under 18,

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.960
So if we can get in a group message

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:01.094
with you and your Abuela, I
would greatly appreciate it.

00:08:01.094 --> 00:08:03.380
I'd love just to be able
to stay in contact with you

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.040
and just support you on your journey,

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.880
because I know a support system is key

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.787
and vital to your success,
so please please please,

00:08:10.787 --> 00:08:12.620
stay in touch with me.

00:08:14.704 --> 00:08:15.547
(everyone applauding)

00:08:15.547 --> 00:08:17.830
- Yes, oh my god, a group
chat with an Olympian.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.432
It's a good day Valeria.

00:08:19.432 --> 00:08:20.996
(Kelly laughs)

